The npm package
---------------

The npm package contains MiniDSH's own files, the adapted material above
among them, and no other project's code. It names one runtime dependency,
zod, which npm installs beside it. zod is under the MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2025 Colin McDonnell.

The desktop installers
----------------------

The four desktop installers (Windows x64, Linux x64 AppImage, macOS arm64,
macOS x64) contain that same npm package and zod, and they also
redistribute binaries built by other projects. MiniDSH 2.0.0 ships:

- Node.js 24.22.3, the official build from nodejs.org, checked against a
  pinned SHA-256 when an installer is made (the pin is in
  desktop/scripts/package.ts and .nvmrc). Only the node executable and its
  LICENSE file are taken from that build. Node.js is under the MIT License.
  Its LICENSE file also carries the licences of the libraries built into it,
  among them V8, OpenSSL, ICU, libuv and zlib.

- Electron 45.4.1 (the pin is the electron entry in package.json), under the
  MIT License, Copyright (c) Electron contributors and Copyright (c)
  2013-2020 GitHub Inc. Electron contains Chromium and the components
  Chromium is built from, each under its own licence. Chromium's credits
  file lists them with their licence texts. One of them, FFmpeg, is under
  the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.

The Windows installer is an NSIS installer made by electron-builder. Its
NSIS target also places resources\elevate.exe in the installed app. No
licence text for that helper ships in the app, and this file states none.

Where the licence texts are in an installed app:

  Windows (%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\minidsh) and Linux (inside the AppImage;
  run it with --appimage-extract to see the files):
    LICENSE.electron.txt                              Electron
    LICENSES.chromium.html                            Chromium's components
    resources/node/LICENSE                            Node.js
    resources/runtime/node_modules/minidsh/LICENSE    MiniDSH
    resources/runtime/node_modules/minidsh/NOTICE     this file
    resources/runtime/node_modules/zod/LICENSE        zod

  macOS: the same six files, all under MiniDSH.app/Contents/Resources/
  (LICENSE.electron.txt and LICENSES.chromium.html directly in it, the rest
  under node/ and runtime/ as above).
